{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The derivative of $h$ can be found using **the power rule**:\n\n$\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^n)=n\\cdot x^{n-1}$\n\n(Remember that this applies even when $n$ is a negative number.)","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}h'(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(x^{-11}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-11x^{-11-1}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{The power rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-11x^{-12}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, we found that $h'(x)=-11x^{-12}$.\n\nThis can also be written as $-\\dfrac{11}{x^{12}}$ (all equivalent forms are accepted).","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $h(x)=x^{-11}$.\n\n$h'(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"-11x^{-12}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
